# Local deviation from vnu 26.8.20 (388cb36): `rev` on <a> is accepted (any
# string), as in vnu's default schema.
#
# Why: rdfa.rnc leaves `rel` and `rev` out of the RDFa attributes of <a>
# (common.attrs.rdfa.no-rel-rev). vnu gets `rev` back from its driver file
# schema/.drivers/legacy.rnc (`a.attrs.rev = attribute rev { string }`,
# `a.attrs &= a.attrs.rev?`), which is not vendored. The definition is copied
# here verbatim. Needed by html-rdfa/0006 and 0007 (expected clean). Not a
# workaround for a missing relax-ng feature.
# File: schema/html5/rdfa.rnc.
#
--- a/rdfa.rnc
+++ b/rdfa.rnc
@@ -170,6 +170,11 @@
 common.attrs &= common.attrs.rdfa

 a.attrs &= common.attrs.rdfa.no-rel-rev
+a.attrs.rev =
+	attribute rev {
+		string
+	}
+a.attrs &= a.attrs.rev?
 area.attrs &= common.attrs.rdfa.no-rel
 base.attrs &= common.attrs.rdfa.no-rel

